# project.mdc — Interview Architect

```yaml
project:
  name: interview-architect
  displayName: Interview Architect
  type: monolith

repositories:
  primary: kritikamodi-17/interview-architect
  modifiable:
    - kritikamodi-17/interview-architect
  readOnly: []
  involved:
    - kritikamodi-17/interview-architect
  localWorkspace: true

technology:
  languages:
    - TypeScript
    - SQL
    - CSS
  languageVersions:
    node: ">=22.0.0"
    typescript: "^5.8.3"
  frameworks:
    - React 19
    - React Router 7
    - Vite 7
    - Hono 4
    - Cloudflare Workers
    - Cloudflare D1
    - Zod 4
    - Vitest 3
    - Playwright 1
  buildTool: npm-workspaces
  testCommands:
    fullSuite: npm run content:validate && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build && npm run test:e2e
    singleClass: npx vitest run <test-file>
  packageRoots:
    - apps/web
    - apps/api
    - packages/content
    - packages/domain
    - infra
    - tests/e2e
  routeConfigPatterns:
    - apps/web/src/App.tsx
    - apps/api/src/app.ts
    - infra/wrangler.jsonc

bugbot:
  enabled: false
  repoUrl: https://github.com/kritikamodi-17/interview-architect
  triggerOnDraftPr: false
  triggerComment: /bugbot
  botLogins: []
  setupDoc: TBD

jira:
  enabled: false
  baseUrl: TBD
  projectKey: TBD
  projectStyle: team-managed
  issueTypes:
    epic: Epic
    story: Story
    task: Task
    subtask: Sub-task

branching:
  defaultBranch: main
  mergeStrategy: merge
  commitConvention: conventional

dependencies:
  internal:
    - '@interview-architect/content'
    - '@interview-architect/domain'
  external:
    - React 19
    - Hono 4
    - Cloudflare D1
    - Zod 4
    - Vite 7
    - Vitest 3
    - Playwright 1

agentVerification:
  runLocally: true
  ciCommands:
    compile: npm run build
    unitTests: npm test
  skipLocal: []
  deferTo:
    - GitHub Actions quality workflow after pull-request push
    - Cloudflare production smoke check after authorized deployment

constraints:
  - Preserve the modular-monolith design; Redis and Kafka are curriculum content, not required runtime infrastructure.
  - Keep anonymous cookie-backed learner identity and the privacy-first default unless the approved SDD explicitly changes it.
  - Do not commit secrets, tokens, .dev.vars, or .env files.
  - Use append-only D1 migrations in infra/migrations for persistent-schema changes.
  - Update both D1Repository and MemoryRepository plus integration tests for repository-interface changes.
  - Keep written answer drafts local by default; any server synchronization needs explicit privacy and deletion behavior.
  - Validate new API input with Zod and use parameterized D1 statements only.
  - Retain strict TypeScript and content validation gates.
  - Do not edit reusable .cursor kit files; only .cursor/project-context is repository-specific.
```
